{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-order quantity limits used by the automatic order-splitting engine.",
    "These are the FALLBACK values: the broker limit resolver first asks the",
    "broker adapter for live limits (fetch_order_limits) and only uses this file",
    "when the broker does not expose them. Adding a new broker requires an entry",
    "here (and optionally an adapter) \u2014 never a change to the execution engine.",
    "",
    "Lookup order: <broker>.<UNDERLYING> -> <broker>.* -> default.",
    "maxLotsPerOrder / maxQtyPerOrder may be null (= no cap on that dimension);",
    "when both are null, or supportsSplitting is false, the order is sent whole.",
    "Values below mirror the exchange freeze limits used by the legacy app",
    "(app/order_manager.py:_get_max_lots_per_order) \u2014 verify against the current",
    "NSE/BSE freeze-quantity circular before relying on them."
  ],
  "default": {
    "*": {
      "maxLotsPerOrder": null,
      "maxQtyPerOrder": null,
      "supportsSplitting": false
    }
  },
